Two bugs: the minute/hour sets are iterated in arbitrary set order, so the earliest matching time isn't chosen (need sorting); and the day-match logic is inverted — when a field starts with `*` its check was skipped instead of performed, so e.g. `* * 1` matched every day and `* * 1-5` (dow) matched every day too. When either field starts with `*`, both fields' value sets must be checked (a `*` field's set is the full range, so it's trivially satisfied); only when neither starts with `*` is it an OR.

